# DMGs are NOT tracked here. They live in GitHub Releases:
#   https://github.com/mindflow-io/mindflow-io.github.io/releases
#
# Until 2026-08-20 this file carried `!Mindflow-latest.dmg`, deliberately
# tracking the rolling DMG because the auto-updater downloaded it from Pages.
# That cost ~77 MB of permanent git history per release — 2.3 GB of blobs
# across 41 commits, 713 MB packed, and Pages deploys over 13 minutes.
# History was rewritten to purge them; VERSION.json now carries a `dmgUrl`
# pointing at the Release asset, and release.sh uploads there instead.
*.dmg

# ─── ONE deliberate exception: the legacy-updater bridge ──────────────────
# Mindflow-latest.dmg is force-added ONCE, frozen at v0.9.2, because every
# client up to v0.9.1 has this Pages URL COMPILED IN (UpdateChecker.swift) and
# cannot be told about the new location. Without it those installs cannot
# auto-update at all — and worse, the 404 would be saved as a fake DMG.
#
# It is FROZEN, not rolling. Do NOT refresh it on future releases:
#   * v0.9.2 is the first build whose updater reads `dmgUrl` from VERSION.json,
#     so an old client only ever needs to reach v0.9.2 — from there the normal
#     Releases path takes over.
#   * A client on, say, v0.9.0 seeing VERSION.json advertise v0.9.5 will fetch
#     this bridge, land on v0.9.2, and then update to v0.9.5 on its next check.
#     Two hops, no bloat.
#   * Refreshing it each release is what cost 2.3 GB the first time.
#
# Safe to delete once nothing older than v0.9.2 is in use.
.DS_Store
